WEBVTT

00:02.500 --> 00:03.800
Ta-dah!

00:03.800 --> 00:05.480
What do you think, Yuki?

00:06.930 --> 00:10.360
I knew it! You try something on, too.

00:13.750 --> 00:15.110
Squee!

00:15.910 --> 00:17.370
You look so good!

00:18.030 --> 00:19.870
So pretty!

00:20.210 --> 00:23.610
Gotta decide what to pack 
for the sign language boot camp, huh?

00:24.780 --> 00:25.620
Hmm?

00:25.620 --> 00:29.130
<b>Sign Language Boot Camp</b>

00:25.620 --> 00:29.130
Saturday, Sign Language
\hBoot Camp, Mountains.

00:26.750 --> 00:29.130
Itsuomi-san doesn't beat around the bush, huh?

00:29.690 --> 00:32.880
That outfit won't suit a trip up the mountains.

00:33.390 --> 00:34.130
Then...

00:34.790 --> 00:38.980
Let's go for a similar look 
with hiking hoodies.

00:38.980 --> 00:42.020
The functional <i>and</i> fashionable one-two punch.

00:42.370 --> 00:45.110
You're so cute!

00:45.390 --> 00:49.020
You're cuter

02:15.230 --> 02:18.990
I Don't Want to Leave

02:20.260 --> 02:21.240
Okay...

02:21.770 --> 02:24.340
That's the outfit problem solved.

02:27.370 --> 02:30.120
<b>Chats</b>

02:27.370 --> 02:30.120
<b>Madoka</b>

02:27.370 --> 02:30.120
<b>Yuki! I asked around about...</b>

02:27.370 --> 02:30.120
<b>Rin</b>

02:27.370 --> 02:30.120
<b>Rin sent a sticker</b>

02:27.370 --> 02:30.120
<b>Boot Camp Chat</b>

02:28.460 --> 02:30.120
<i>Oh, Madoka-chan.</i>

02:30.170 --> 02:35.630
You're gonna work too?! Yay!
Okay, I gotchu!

02:31.020 --> 02:35.180
<i>I did ask her if she knew any good part-
time jobs. Is she messaging about that?</i>

02:36.630 --> 02:44.140
Yuki! I asked around
about jobs!

02:36.860 --> 02:41.230
<i>Yuki! I asked around about jobs!</i>

02:40.890 --> 02:44.140
I think I found
a good one.

02:41.230 --> 02:43.370
<i>I think I found a good one.</i>

02:50.020 --> 02:51.650
Yeah. The person working
part-time now at my relative's
café is going to quit soon
to job hunt for real.

02:50.020 --> 02:51.650
I'll contact you
when that happens!

02:50.020 --> 02:51.650
Sure, thanks! I'll be waiting!

02:50.020 --> 02:51.650
I Leave It in Thy Hands

02:52.130 --> 02:55.460
<i>I need this to travel with Itsuomi-san!</i>

02:55.460 --> 02:57.540
<i>Please, let me land a job!</i>

03:00.260 --> 03:03.530
Oh... Sorry, what?

03:03.780 --> 03:08.540
Is something wrong?
You look down.

03:05.320 --> 03:08.540
Oh, yeah, kind of.

03:09.030 --> 03:12.000
Remember how I was working over spring break?

03:12.000 --> 03:16.550
One of my colleagues there 
keeps asking me out to dinner.

03:16.880 --> 03:18.930
His name's Tsujimura.

03:18.930 --> 03:21.210
He helped me out big time with work.

03:21.930 --> 03:28.680
Do you think he's interested?

03:23.490 --> 03:28.680
Hmm... Well, I think I'll pass on 
going out alone with him.

03:29.050 --> 03:32.050
<i>Of course Rin-chan would be popular.</i>

03:32.050 --> 03:35.230
Nothing from Kyouya-san.

03:35.690 --> 03:40.710
Will you help me get some alone time 
with him during the boot camp?

03:41.980 --> 03:45.070
I guess you two'll get some 
alone time then, too.

03:47.580 --> 03:50.510
Man, I can't wait for Saturday!

03:54.210 --> 03:56.710
The day has come!

03:57.210 --> 03:59.840
We're here to get you, Rin-chan, Yuki-chan.

04:00.120 --> 04:01.700
Hello!

04:01.700 --> 04:05.590
I'm glad it's so nice out. 
Perfect weather for an outing.

04:05.590 --> 04:10.200
Whaddaya think, Itsuomi-san? 
We went for a matching look!

04:10.200 --> 04:11.890
Yeah, that's pretty similar.

04:11.890 --> 04:13.550
That's your reaction?

04:13.550 --> 04:15.350
I like it. Very cute.

04:15.350 --> 04:17.610
<i>Whoo! Surprise attack!</i>

04:18.110 --> 04:19.810
Hurry up and get in.

04:19.810 --> 04:21.200
'Kay!

04:24.070 --> 04:25.050
Get in front.

04:28.570 --> 04:28.990
<i>I...</i>

04:29.770 --> 04:31.800
<i>Itsuomi-san's driving?</i>

04:32.850 --> 04:36.740
No rash driving, please, Itsuomi-san!

04:36.740 --> 04:37.420
Sure.

04:39.670 --> 04:43.050
<i>Would it be distracting 
if I stared at him too much?</i>

04:44.030 --> 04:45.760
<i>I should look outside.</i>

04:46.210 --> 04:49.550
<i>It'll be hard to communicate, but oh well.</i>

05:02.260 --> 05:03.420
Yuki.

05:04.650 --> 05:08.330
I thought of a game we can 
all play during the drive.

05:08.330 --> 05:10.530
It's Wish Word Chain.

05:10.530 --> 05:13.540
<b>I thought of a game we can all play during the drive.



First up, Wish Word Chain



Flip the page!!</b>

05:10.980 --> 05:12.310
<i>Rin-chan...</i>

05:14.120 --> 05:16.660
<i>She's so thoughtful.</i>

05:19.040 --> 05:30.800
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

05:19.040 --> 05:30.800
<b>Rules
* Each player writes a wish into the sketchbook.
\h\hThe wishes must form a word chain.
* Respond to the other players' wishes
\h\hwith a thumbs-up gesture.
* I (Rin) will write for whoever's driving.</b>

05:19.350 --> 05:22.720
We'll play a game of word chain 
by writing our wishes.

05:22.720 --> 05:25.380
Respond to the other players' 
wishes with a "Nice."

05:26.050 --> 05:29.220
Itsuomi-san, say yours out loud, 
and I'll jot it down.

05:29.220 --> 05:30.800
Huh...

05:31.100 --> 05:33.300
Okay, let me start!

05:33.300 --> 05:35.560
Find a D.C. I can fave!

05:33.640 --> 05:35.560
<b>Find a D.C. I can fave</b>

05:37.210 --> 05:38.560
Nice.

05:38.560 --> 05:41.230
Sorry, what's a D.C.?

05:41.230 --> 05:43.840
"Drugstore cosmetic."

05:43.840 --> 05:46.560
They're petit-priced.

05:46.560 --> 05:47.820
Petit-priced...?

05:48.180 --> 05:50.830
You're next, Kyouya-san. Start with "E."

05:51.180 --> 05:52.980
Okay...

05:53.950 --> 05:57.410
<b>Find a D.C. I can fave

Enter a brand-new cocktail into the bar lineup</b>

05:54.190 --> 05:57.410
"Enter a brand-new cocktail 
into the bar lineup."

05:57.410 --> 05:59.620
Ooh, nice.

05:59.620 --> 06:02.440
Very nice. I'd like to try it!

06:02.440 --> 06:04.670
Okay, Yuki-chan's turn.

06:04.670 --> 06:09.430
<b>Purchase a cute new pair of shoes</b>

06:05.480 --> 06:08.130
"Purchase a cute new pair of shoes."

06:08.130 --> 06:09.910
Nice!

06:12.890 --> 06:13.770
Nice.

06:14.590 --> 06:16.820
Now it's you, Itsuomi-san.

06:16.820 --> 06:18.980
Start with "S."

06:19.950 --> 06:20.870
Hmm...

06:21.540 --> 06:24.690
Set off overseas on a trip with my girlfriend.

06:26.440 --> 06:29.860
Nice, nice! Yeah, hurry up and go!

06:29.860 --> 06:31.200
Look, Yuki!

06:34.820 --> 06:39.810
<i>He's looking forward to traveling with me.</i>

06:40.750 --> 06:42.660
<i>I need to find a job soon.</i>

06:43.460 --> 06:47.340
<b>Saturday, April 13</b>

06:44.120 --> 06:46.980
<i>But I haven't heard back 
from Madoka-chan yet...</i>

06:53.780 --> 06:55.860
The tent's all done!

06:55.860 --> 06:57.930
Oh, great!

06:58.370 --> 07:00.330
It's like we're at a luxury camp.

07:00.750 --> 07:01.890
Did we need the flags?

07:01.890 --> 07:02.940
We so did!

07:03.400 --> 07:06.090
Okay, let me get lunch started.

07:06.500 --> 07:07.370
Sure.

07:08.580 --> 07:10.560
I'm so excited now!

07:10.560 --> 07:11.780
Hey.

07:12.740 --> 07:15.370
We're starting the sign lessons.

07:16.790 --> 07:20.020
Yuki, how do you sign "mountain"?

07:20.020 --> 07:21.540
Moun-tain!

07:21.540 --> 07:23.670
Is that how you always ask?

07:23.670 --> 07:25.990
<i>That's so him.</i>

07:27.330 --> 07:28.460
<i>Mountain...</i>

07:29.640 --> 07:30.370
And this?

07:31.470 --> 07:32.680
<b>Rock</b>

07:31.500 --> 07:32.680
<i>Rock.</i>

07:32.930 --> 07:34.300
And this?

07:35.000 --> 07:36.430
<i>Smartphone.</i>

07:35.220 --> 07:36.430
<b>swipe</b>

07:37.140 --> 07:38.180
How about "river"?

07:40.460 --> 07:41.440
And "tent"?

07:51.770 --> 07:52.630
Now this?

07:53.200 --> 07:54.840
Eek!

07:54.840 --> 07:57.330
Let it go!

07:57.640 --> 08:00.970
Hey, how about a break?

08:05.790 --> 08:07.650
Yum!

08:07.650 --> 08:09.460
I put some serious effort into this.

08:11.150 --> 08:12.060
Like it?

08:14.260 --> 08:16.460
So that's how you say "it's delicious."

08:16.970 --> 08:20.970
I don't know if I can commit everything 
I learned today to memory.

08:21.450 --> 08:23.260
We'll have a pop quiz later.

08:23.260 --> 08:24.460
Seriously?

08:24.460 --> 08:25.150
Of course.

08:25.150 --> 08:26.230
Eep.

08:26.570 --> 08:31.240
<i>They were talking so fast, 
I couldn't read their lips in time.</i>

08:38.780 --> 08:39.490
This...

08:40.390 --> 08:41.140
is good.

08:43.090 --> 08:45.550
Way to show off, guys.

08:45.550 --> 08:49.450
Rin-chan, why don't we go explore 
for a bit when we're done eating?

08:49.450 --> 08:51.760
Oh, good idea.

08:54.260 --> 08:57.120
Looks like things are going well between them.

08:57.120 --> 08:58.540
Right?

08:59.310 --> 09:01.370
Do you have anyone like that?

09:01.370 --> 09:04.660
Huh? Like, a boyfriend?

09:06.940 --> 09:09.770
<b></b>Tsujimura-san

09:06.940 --> 09:09.770
<b></b>Cellphone

09:07.310 --> 09:09.300
Ack! Why?!

09:09.770 --> 09:11.450
Sorry, I gotta take this!

09:11.450 --> 09:12.170
Sure.

09:13.210 --> 09:14.210
Hello?

09:14.940 --> 09:17.770
Oh, Rin-chan? 
Sorry for calling out of the blue.

09:17.770 --> 09:18.660
Hey, so...

09:19.110 --> 09:22.340
Listen! I'm kinda busy right now...

09:22.340 --> 09:25.140
<i>Oh, I guess I called at a bad time.</i>

09:26.870 --> 09:29.420
Can I call you back later?

09:29.730 --> 09:34.140
Well, if it's to invite me out again,

09:34.140 --> 09:36.220
I would appreciate it if you didn't.

09:36.220 --> 09:41.260
<i>Oh... Do you already have someone in mind?</i>

09:41.260 --> 09:44.430
<i>Kyouya-san's right behind me!</i>

09:47.740 --> 09:48.810
That's right.

09:49.940 --> 09:52.510
I'm in love with someone.

09:53.570 --> 09:57.260
Well, that's how it is. I have to go now.

10:01.970 --> 10:04.090
Sorry about that.

10:04.520 --> 10:06.080
I knew you'd be popular.

10:06.080 --> 10:06.830
Huh?

10:07.270 --> 10:10.580
Sorry, I overheard a little 
of the conversation.

10:10.580 --> 10:12.300
I'm really not!

10:12.300 --> 10:17.490
I've... only ever gone out with one person.

10:17.490 --> 10:20.890
What about you, Kyouya-san? 
Did your relationships last long?

10:21.310 --> 10:24.720
Yeah. The longest was about six years.

10:24.720 --> 10:25.560
Six?!

10:26.070 --> 10:29.250
A-Are you looking now?

10:29.690 --> 10:31.790
When you get to be my age,

10:31.790 --> 10:37.040
the whole process of texting and going 
on dates starts to become kind of a pain.

10:37.040 --> 10:38.820
Is that how it is?

10:39.460 --> 10:44.340
So I'd have to really fall for someone 
to go through all that again.

10:45.410 --> 10:47.000
<i>You're...</i>

10:47.990 --> 10:51.730
<i>You're free to fall for me all you like.</i>

10:55.090 --> 10:55.880
Say.

10:59.340 --> 11:03.410
Who's this person you're in love with?

11:05.600 --> 11:07.350
<b>Make a Reservation</b>

11:05.600 --> 11:07.350
<b></b>New Spring Menu

11:08.020 --> 11:10.250
<i>It's not Madoka-chan...</i>

11:16.070 --> 11:17.900
<i>Huh? Itsuomi-san?!</i>

11:29.430 --> 11:30.500
It got away.

11:37.160 --> 11:38.630
Don't force yourself.

11:39.020 --> 11:42.650
It's only April. Of course the water's cold.

11:46.250 --> 11:47.890
Timber!

11:58.350 --> 12:00.050
<i>The purest laughter.</i>

12:00.940 --> 12:03.500
<i>Would he mind if I said it was cute?</i>

12:06.810 --> 12:11.650
<i>The trust I have in him to never drop me 
makes my heart race in a different way.</i>

12:12.180 --> 12:14.620
<i>If people get a finite stock 
of luck in their lifetime,</i>

12:15.020 --> 12:17.020
<i>I feel like I've used up way too much of it.</i>

12:23.370 --> 12:25.090
Your feet are cold.

12:27.620 --> 12:30.600
Yuki, is something bothering you?

12:32.770 --> 12:35.770
I haven't been able
to land a job...

12:34.820 --> 12:35.770
Oh.

12:36.020 --> 12:41.530
But a friend of mine
said she had a lead.

12:38.520 --> 12:41.530
I've just been checking my phone
waiting for her to contact me.

12:40.410 --> 12:41.090
Mm.

12:43.150 --> 12:45.530
If what I said during the drive
put more pressure on you,
I apologize.

12:48.030 --> 12:50.410
<b></b>I'm looking forward to it

12:48.030 --> 12:50.410
<b></b>I'm looking forward to it

12:50.540 --> 12:53.040
<b></b>way more than you are.

12:50.540 --> 12:53.040
<b></b>way more than you are.

12:54.410 --> 12:56.540
<b></b>More than me?

12:54.410 --> 12:56.540
<b></b>More than me?

12:56.900 --> 13:00.300
What makes you say that?

13:01.770 --> 13:02.930
<i>Why...</i>

13:03.660 --> 13:07.620
<i>Why is he so good at giving me butterflies?</i>

13:08.540 --> 13:14.570
<i>It's still bright and sunny out, and I 
already feel bad that this day will end.</i>

13:22.260 --> 13:24.570
What do you wanna do later?

13:44.670 --> 13:47.400
Do you have to go home tonight?

13:48.610 --> 13:51.630
I don't want to let you go yet.

14:05.630 --> 14:07.000
<i>He just pinched my cheek.</i>

14:07.740 --> 14:11.550
<i>Is he giving me the signal 
like he said he would?</i>

14:35.710 --> 14:37.620
Sorry!

14:37.620 --> 14:40.100
I might have injured my ankle...

14:41.270 --> 14:42.990
Wait, you're hurt?

14:42.990 --> 14:46.640
Well... I may have gotten 
a teensy bit too excited.

14:46.640 --> 14:49.420
Oh... so you two were getting handsy.

14:49.420 --> 14:51.700
That's not it—

14:51.700 --> 14:53.780
Oww...

14:54.080 --> 14:55.220
Are you okay?

14:55.730 --> 14:58.290
I'll take her to a hospital right away.

14:58.590 --> 14:59.960
What about you two?

15:01.320 --> 15:02.250
Let's go with, yeah?

15:03.160 --> 15:05.690
I'm sorry!

15:05.690 --> 15:08.800
Rest up in the car. We'll clean up here.

15:13.140 --> 15:14.500
Here, water.

15:14.500 --> 15:16.310
Oh, sorry.

15:16.700 --> 15:20.060
I'd prefer it if you thanked me instead.

15:21.020 --> 15:22.810
Thank you very much.

15:24.250 --> 15:26.820
So, hey... about earlier...

15:28.460 --> 15:31.820
<i>Who's this person you're in love with?</i>

15:32.550 --> 15:38.540
I've been around the block enough times 
to know not to jump to conclusions.

15:39.340 --> 15:41.080
But when I spend time with you,

15:42.100 --> 15:44.900
sometimes I just get the feeling I'm right.

15:45.910 --> 15:50.340
Would it... be a problem if you were?

15:50.620 --> 15:52.220
Of course not!

15:52.220 --> 15:55.680
I mean, you did say 
you find dating to be a pain.

15:55.680 --> 15:58.100
In any other situation, sure!

15:59.210 --> 16:01.950
Please tell me straight up.

16:04.870 --> 16:09.050
I wouldn't find it a pain at all with you.

16:10.510 --> 16:14.530
Honestly, seeing you get a call 
from another guy didn't feel good.

16:15.080 --> 16:17.070
I thought about laughing it off,

16:18.280 --> 16:22.010
but deep down, I'm stupidly childish.

16:22.840 --> 16:24.250
And super cringe.

16:24.250 --> 16:27.590
No way! You're not the least bit cringe...

16:27.590 --> 16:31.500
Gah!

16:32.590 --> 16:36.080
I ruined it <i>all</i>! I hate myself!

16:36.080 --> 16:37.850
It's fine.

16:38.630 --> 16:41.290
Besides, it made me happy.

16:43.420 --> 16:46.350
Rin-chan, I think you're very charming.

16:46.680 --> 16:47.710
Huh?

16:47.710 --> 16:50.460
Okay, I'm gonna go help them pack things up.

16:51.340 --> 16:52.360
Okay...

17:01.420 --> 17:04.670
<i>It was short-lived, but I had fun.</i>

17:07.500 --> 17:10.000
<b></b>Let's all come back sometime!

17:24.730 --> 17:26.960
Okay, off to the hospital we go.

17:26.960 --> 17:29.400
Sure. Take care, Rin.

17:29.660 --> 17:32.110
I'll contact you later.

17:32.110 --> 17:33.900
Uh... Okay?

17:33.900 --> 17:35.650
Why do you sound like you hate the idea?!

17:36.040 --> 17:38.160
I mean, you finally get some alone time.

17:43.640 --> 17:45.210
It's still only 6 PM.

17:45.770 --> 17:49.970
Okay, let's continue the boot camp. 
Just the two of us.

17:50.920 --> 17:53.420
<b>Izakaya Maru</b>

17:58.180 --> 18:03.180
<b>Yakitori</b>

17:58.180 --> 18:03.180
<b>Beer</b>

18:12.940 --> 18:16.950
<b>Izakaya Maru</b>

18:14.910 --> 18:16.610
Thank you! Come again!

18:17.260 --> 18:18.870
<i>That was fun.</i>

18:19.560 --> 18:23.560
9 PM, huh? Wanna hit up the convenience store 
before heading back?

18:28.930 --> 18:30.960
<i>Itsuomi-san's place!</i>

18:31.610 --> 18:34.370
<i>He did say he didn't want to let me go...</i>

18:35.050 --> 18:35.780
<i>Wait!</i>

18:38.130 --> 18:39.970
Today

18:38.130 --> 18:39.970
I'm staying the night at Rin-chan's place

18:43.470 --> 18:44.770
Here, freshen up.

18:45.570 --> 18:49.230
We're just gonna be spending time together.

18:49.900 --> 18:51.430
Don't be so nervous.

19:02.300 --> 19:04.490
I'm gonna go ahead and take a shower.

19:04.840 --> 19:06.580
What? I have to undress over there?

19:07.050 --> 19:09.560
Okay, okay. You should change, too.

19:13.340 --> 19:15.770
<i>I went and borrowed his clothes...</i>

19:16.450 --> 19:18.260
<i>They're so baggy.</i>

19:19.380 --> 19:24.710
<i>I smell softener we don't use at home, along 
with Itsuomi-san's scent mixed in with it.</i>

19:27.170 --> 19:29.900
<i>I'm happy I got to come here again.</i>

19:33.650 --> 19:36.400
<b>Sign Language Guide</b>

19:34.600 --> 19:36.400
<i>Oh, the Sign Language Guide!</i>

19:36.400 --> 19:38.150
<b>Using phones, handwriting, or gestures.</b>

19:36.400 --> 19:38.150
<b>Sometimes through <u>mouthing</u>.</b>

19:36.400 --> 19:38.150
<b>Like lipreading?</b>

19:37.550 --> 19:40.270
<i>We used it to go back and forth that one time.</i>

19:45.660 --> 19:49.410
<b>Go home</b>

19:45.660 --> 19:49.410
<b>Separate the thumb and other fingers
\hbefore bringing them together
\h\hin a mouth-closing motion.</b>

19:45.660 --> 19:49.410
<b></b>Buy

19:45.660 --> 19:49.410
<b></b>*Reverse

19:45.660 --> 19:49.410
<b></b>Sell

19:46.790 --> 19:49.090
<i>Is this Itsuomi-san's handwriting?</i>

19:53.670 --> 19:57.420
<b>Overseas</b>

19:53.670 --> 19:57.420
<b>Can also mean "foreigner"
or "the West"</b>

19:53.670 --> 19:57.420
<b>Trip</b>

19:53.670 --> 19:57.420
<b>Picture a steam engine's wheels</b>

19:56.460 --> 20:00.920
<b>Rain</b>

19:56.460 --> 20:00.920
<b>Gesture changes slightly
depending on the type of rain</b>

19:58.340 --> 20:00.220
<i>He's written so many notes.</i>

20:01.380 --> 20:08.090
<i>Come to think of it, he pretty much always 
gets the signs I've taught him perfect.</i>

20:08.430 --> 20:10.680
<b>Snow</b>

20:08.430 --> 20:10.680
<b>Make a circle with your fingers
and bring your hands down,
shaking them alternately</b>

20:10.680 --> 20:14.190
<b>Sign Language Guide</b>

20:15.460 --> 20:16.760
You know, Oushi.

20:17.480 --> 20:21.950
It's great how dogs wear their 
hearts on their sleeves, huh?

20:22.690 --> 20:23.640
Huh?

20:24.550 --> 20:29.070
You came to say something 
to me, right? Spit it out.

20:38.550 --> 20:39.460
This evening...

20:40.360 --> 20:45.860
I saw Yuki-san and what seemed 
like her boyfriend walk into a pub.

20:47.720 --> 20:50.100
<b>Saving...</b>

20:48.530 --> 20:49.580
Boyfriend?

20:50.100 --> 20:51.140
<b>Save complete</b>

20:52.120 --> 20:55.090
So what? It won't last.

20:55.740 --> 20:57.400
And you're okay with that?

20:57.990 --> 20:59.480
What are you trying to say?

21:01.860 --> 21:06.460
That guy was using a bit of sign.

21:06.970 --> 21:07.930
Sign...

21:09.530 --> 21:11.480
Did he have silver hair?

21:11.960 --> 21:13.110
You know him?

21:13.960 --> 21:16.250
You came over just to tell me that?

21:16.250 --> 21:17.380
No!

21:30.230 --> 21:33.170
You should be more upfront with your feelings.

21:34.380 --> 21:37.910
The way you are right now 
is painful for me to watch.

22:01.250 --> 22:03.250
<b></b>Oushi
Video Call

22:06.010 --> 22:10.010
I Don't Want to Leave

23:15.030 --> 23:30.260
Oushi's World
